    "Same structure as content/routines/strong-foundations-6-weeks.json. Exercise details live in content/exercises/strength-catalogue.json.",
    "Each phase defines its day templates; every week in that phase repeats them.",
    "Lighter week: use about 60 to 70% of the normal sets (round down, minimum 1) at the same weights, with 3 reps in reserve.",
    "Exercises sharing a superset_group are done back to back, resting after the pair.",
    "Draft for coach review before launch.",
    "Complete week: her onboarding days-per-week is the number of gym days she can do. Never plan more gym days than that.",
    "Complete week: weekly_plan.strength_days go on her chosen days in order. Finishers (by profiles.cardio_preference) are a cardio block after the strength block on that day; skipped in skip_weeks (checkpoint and lighter weeks) and skippable with one tap.",
    "Complete week: if she picked more days than gym_days_needed, fill the spare days with spare_day_cardio for her preference, in order (CARDIO1 first). Avoid placing cardio the day before a lower-body day where possible. If she picked fewer days than strength_days, recommend a different routine instead.",
    "Complete week: anytime_extras (the recovery stretch) aren't tied to a day. Show them as 'Anytime this week' in the Planner. They're optional.",
    "Complete week: cardio_balanced routines need gym_days_needed days (strength plus required_cardio_days). Only recommend them when she picked at least that many days.",
    "Complete week: her weekly target is her onboarding days-per-week. Any session counts towards it (strength, cardio, or a stretch or recovery session of 10+ minutes). schedule_label is the line shown on the routine page; the card shows '{days_per_week} days a week' (or gym_days_needed for cardio_balanced routines)."
